index cf475bf..03069eb 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -41,6 +41,25 @@ RelayBoard is a small job-control application with:
 
 The implementation should remain small enough that a reviewer can inspect the whole system.
 
+## Pausing Jobs
+
+`POST /api/jobs/{id}/pause` and `POST /api/jobs/{id}/resume` take no body and
+return HTTP 200 with `{"job": ...}`, including the Job's boolean `paused` field.
+Both operations are idempotent. An unknown Job returns HTTP 404 using the
+existing error format. `GET /api/jobs` also includes `paused`.
+
+A paused Job rejects new scheduled Runs with HTTP 409 until resumed. Manual
+Runs remain allowed. Existing Runs continue accepting Attempts and retries and
+retain the existing alert behavior. Pause does not change the Job's `enabled`
+setting: resuming a disabled Job leaves scheduling disabled, and enabling a
+paused Job leaves it paused. Resume does not create a Run or replay missed work.
+
+The dashboard displays Paused separately from Enabled and preserves Last result.
+Pause state is stored with the Job; existing databases receive a default-false
+column when opened by `Store`.
+
+Verify with `python -m unittest discover -s tests -v`.
+
 ## Treatment isolation
 
 Treatment agents receive the fixture workspace and scenario prompt.
